  "claims": [
    "A note written with 25 or fewer ignored paths is byte-for-byte the note main writes.",
    "takeover reports ready only if every ignored path the note was written with, other than a key file, exists in the checkout, wherever it sits in the list and whatever characters it holds.",
    "A note from 0.1.3 or older whose list was cut, and any ignored-rest line that is damaged, short, long, nested or not a list of path and kind items, gives ready false and never raises.",
    "A path holding a newline or other control character cannot make a note read as ready while that path is missing.",
    "A commit subject, file name or other text shaped like the ignored-files heading does not move where takeover reads the ignored section.",
    "A missing key file, listed or after the 25th, is reported in missing_keys and does not block.",
    "plugins/ is rebuilt from skills/ at 0.1.4."
  ],
